cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AOBench, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "AOBench: A Trace-Driven, Role-Aware Benchmark for Agent Operations in Realistic Environments"
abstract: >-
  AOBench (Agent Operations Benchmark) is an open-source Python benchmark
  framework for evaluating AI agents that operate High-Performance Computing
  (HPC) systems. It measures whether an agent completes HPC operational tasks —
  job scheduling, telemetry interpretation, energy reasoning, and policy
  enforcement — using the right tools, roles, and permissions. Every task is
  evaluated against a deterministic environment snapshot with mock HPC tools
  (SLURM, telemetry, RBAC, docs, facility), so results are role-aware,
  permission-enforced, trace-based, and reproducible.
type: software
